# Task 06 — Auth: initData → session (Phase 1, 9h)

RFC anchors: §11 (auth chain + edge cases), §27.6 (bearer payload format),
§13.1 session endpoint, §13.5 throttles, D21/D32.

## Goal

`POST /tgapp/api/v1/session` exchanges Telegram initData for a 12 h encrypted
bearer; middleware guards `/tgapp/api/v1/*` and resolves `TgUiContext`'s
identity half.

## Read first

- `menu.md` §11 verbatim (validation steps, freshness windows,
  edge-case table, revocation ladder), §27.6 items 2–3, §27.8 throttle
  buckets, §27.9 dispatch ladder steps 1–3.

## Deliverables

1. `Auth\InitDataValidator` — pure PHP: parse initData; recompute
   `secret = HMAC_SHA256(bot_token, "WebAppData")`,
   `hash = HMAC_SHA256(initData, secret)`; constant-time compare;
   freshness `auth_date ≥ now−24h` and `≤ now+120s`; reject missing user /
   present-but-invalid desktop `signature`. Official Telegram test vectors +
   negative matrix (tampered hash, stale, future, foreign-bot token, missing
   user, bad signature) as unit tests.
2. `Auth\SessionIssuer` — mints `Crypt::encryptString` bearer with EXACT key
   set from §27.6 item 2 (`bot, uid, name, photo, locale, iat, ep, exp`),
   `exp = min(now+12h, auth_date+24h)`, `ep = tg.app.sessionEpoch.{bot}`.
   Verify signed `startappCtx` per D32 algorithm from golden fixtures (task
   04); bind chatId as navigation hint only. Session response `hints.bots`
   block (§13.2) reads `tg_menu_bot_settings` NULL-safely — row/table may be
   absent pre-install ⇒ username/appSlug returned as null; NEVER call getMe
   on this path (F7 discipline extends to session: no auxiliary TG calls on
   auth hot path either).
3. `Console\SessionsRevokeCommand` (`tg:menu:sessions:revoke {bot}`) → epoch
   INCR.
4. `Http\Laravel\TgAppSessionMiddleware` — decrypt bearer on every
   `/tgapp/api/v1/*`; bot binding (IDOR guard); epoch compare (mismatch ⇒ 401,
   SPA re-handshakes); attach attributes + resolved refs onto the request so
   the context middleware (task 09, §27.9 step 3) assembles `TgUiContext`;
   echo `X-TgApp-Request-Id` — client-supplied ids echoed only when matching
   `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,64}$`, otherwise replaced by a server-generated id
   (log-injection safety, §11). First check in the pipeline (§27.9 step 0):
   `config('menu.maintenance')` true ⇒ 503 `degraded` envelope before any
   session work (D46) — asserted by test with the flag on.
5. Controller endpoint wiring in host `../../../../../routes/web.php` group (session route +
   limiter registration in AppServiceProvider reading `config('menu.throttle.*')`)
   — ALL FOUR named buckets from §27.8, not just the session one:
   `tgapp-session` keyed by client IP + sha256-prefix of initData (pre-auth),
   `tgapp-read` / `tgapp-write` / `tgapp-api` keyed by authenticated tg uid.
   Later tasks (09/11) only reference these buckets — nobody re-registers.
6. Tests: `InitDataValidatorTest`, `SessionTokenTest` (roundtrip/expiry/
    foreign-bot/APP_KEY rotation/epoch bump), feature test for the endpoint
    incl. throttle and edge cases from §11 table (photo_url scheme check is a
    frontend/CSP concern — server only validates https prefix if present;
    requestId sanitization matrix: valid id echoed, junk regenerated), plus a
    bucket matrix test asserting all four limiters exist with configured
    limits and correct keys.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Golden fixture vectors from task 04 pass through the real validator.
- [ ] Session cannot outlive initData validity (boundary tests at both caps).
- [ ] Epoch bump invalidates outstanding tokens immediately (401 → client
      re-handshake path asserted).
- [ ] Throttle returns 429 with Retry-After after limit.

## Verification

```
php artisan test --compact --filter='InitData|Session'
```

## Guardrails

Secrets never logged; `hash_equals` everywhere; §11 honest-model notes are
contract comments where relevant (D21).

## Completion notes (2026-08-26)

- All deliverables landed: `Auth\InitDataValidator` (pure PHP, INV-4),
  `Auth\SessionIssuer` (+ `BearerPayload`/`TgIssuedSession`/`TgInitDataUser`
  DTOs), `Auth\StartappCtxVerifier` (D32), `Http\Laravel` adapters
  (`CryptBearerEncrypter`, `CacheSessionEpochStore`, `TgAppSessionMiddleware`,
  `TgAppSessionController`), `Console\SessionsRevokeCommand`, host route
  block + four named throttle buckets in AppServiceProvider.
- INV-4 purity kept: Auth core receives encryption and epoch storage through
  menu-package contracts (`TgBearerEncrypterContract`,
  `TgSessionEpochStoreContract`); Laravel types live only in Http/Laravel.
- Ladder fidelity (§27.9): the middleware alias supports two modes — `gate`
  (step 0 maintenance + request-id bookkeeping) and `auth` (bearer decrypt,
  bot binding, epoch compare). Host stacks run `tgapp.session:gate` →
  `throttle:*` → `tgapp.session:auth` so maintenance precedes throttling
  which precedes bearer work. Request-id attribute is reused across passes.
- Telegram algorithm notes verified against core.telegram.org/bots/webapps:
  bot-side HMAC keeps the desktop `signature` field INSIDE the check-string;
  third-party signature is base64url Ed25519 over "{bot_id}:WebAppData\n" +
  fields minus hash/signature; production pubkey
  `e7bf03a2…caed242d` shipped as `menu.session.thirdparty_public_key`
  default (empty ⇒ fail-open tolerance documented in §11). The docs carry no
  concrete HMAC vector, so the unit suite pins a self-computed golden vector
  (WireFixtures-style) plus an independent builder cross-check.
- Config delta: `session.thirdparty_public_key` added to the §27.8 tree
  (additive; needed to make desktop-signature verification configurable per
  environment).
- Multi-bot session minting: initData does not name its bot; candidates are
  tried in bot_id order, first verifying token wins. Tokens never logged.
- Acceptance evidence: golden ctx vectors pass the real verifier; boundary
  tests at both exp caps (12 h / auth_date+24 h); epoch bump → immediate 401
  then re-mint; APP_KEY rotation → 401 (container+facade re-resolve);
  throttle 429 with Retry-After; maintenance flag → 503 degraded before any
  session work; requestId sanitize matrix. Suites: menu-unit + menu-feature
  91 passed (266 assertions); combined lib+menu+management run 704 passed.
- Pre-existing repairs made to keep tooling runnable: phpstan.neon.dist /
  phpstan-baseline.neon paths updated for the telegram-bot-mafia-module →
  telegram-game-mafia directory rename (all referenced files verified
  present). Remaining known-red (untouched, out of scope): host phpstan
  reports Route::inertia() stub gaps + routes/console.php undefined var;
  deps/check flags proxy-module layout, game-mafia composer-name/suite and a
  stale composer.prod.lock.

